\name{cellucid_analysis_detailed_set}
\alias{cellucid_analysis_detailed_set}
\title{Choose what the detailed analysis plots}
\usage{
cellucid_analysis_detailed_set(viewer, in_ = "panel", plot, plot_options, variable)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{in_}{Either exactly \code{"panel"} (The Analysis panel); or a whole number (at least 1) (A floating analysis window, by its number (1 is the first open)). Default \code{"panel"}, the viewer's own. Sent as the parameter \code{in}.}
\item{plot}{The plot, by its id as the Plot select offers it for the variable's kind. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{plot_options}{Options of the plot, each by its name and value. A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{variable}{What to plot: a column of the cells (categorical_obs, continuous_obs) or a gene (gene_expression) by name, or null for nothing. Either \code{NULL}; or a named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does). \describe{\item{\code{key}}{Text (at least 1 character). Required.}\item{\code{type}}{One of \code{"categorical_obs"}, \code{"continuous_obs"}, \code{"gene_expression"}. Required.}}}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
The variable the detailed analysis plots (a field or a gene, by name, or none), the plot, and options of that plot (only those given); it updates by itself.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{analysis.detailed.set} (Analysis). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{analysis}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_analysis_detailed_set(viewer, variable = list(key = "cell_type",
      type = "categorical_obs"))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
